WEBVTT

00:00:07.750 --> 00:00:11.333
<i>Fluttering and dancing in the sky</i>

00:00:11.333 --> 00:00:17.708
<i>Let our love reach you...</i>

00:00:17.708 --> 00:00:18.458
<i>LOVE,</i>

00:00:18.458 --> 00:00:19.542
<i>LOVE,</i>

00:00:19.542 --> 00:00:20.958
<i>LOVE...</i>

00:00:23.167 --> 00:00:25.000
<i>ohhhh... SAY!</i>

00:00:25.000 --> 00:00:26.417
<i>This heart</i>

00:00:26.417 --> 00:00:28.708
<i>Try and move it</i>

00:00:28.708 --> 00:00:31.833
<i>Look, how should I show you?</i>

00:00:31.833 --> 00:00:33.000
<i>Then together with us</i>

00:00:33.000 --> 00:00:34.375
<i>Let's dance! Take my hand</i>

00:00:34.375 --> 00:00:35.833
<i>hey yeah yeah!</i>

00:00:35.833 --> 00:00:37.333
<i>Leave it to me</i>

00:00:37.333 --> 00:00:40.250
<i>to escort you! ALL RIGHT!</i>

00:00:40.250 --> 00:00:42.958
<i>As if worrying, the passing rain</i>

00:00:42.958 --> 00:00:46.417
<i>caressed my cheek gently,</i>
<i>so as not to be noticed.</i>

00:00:46.417 --> 00:00:50.375
<i>Jumping over faster than a shooting star</i>

00:00:50.375 --> 00:00:53.833
<i>Reach out your hand!</i>

00:00:53.833 --> 00:00:54.750
<i>let's get LOVE!</i>

00:00:54.750 --> 00:00:56.375
<i>Shout to the moon! (shout!)</i>

00:00:56.375 --> 00:00:58.000
<i>Let your shout ring out! (shout!)</i>

00:00:58.000 --> 00:00:59.167
<i>What's up, what's up?</i>

00:00:59.167 --> 00:01:00.917
<i>Let me hear your voice</i>

00:01:00.917 --> 00:01:02.458
<i>Undo your hair</i>

00:01:02.458 --> 00:01:05.458
<i>Saying goodbye to yesterday</i>

00:01:05.458 --> 00:01:06.458
<i>when my eyes were closed</i>

00:01:06.458 --> 00:01:09.000
<i>A single petal fluttering lightly</i>

00:01:09.000 --> 00:01:10.875
<i>Spit it out, SHOUT! (shout!)</i>

00:01:10.875 --> 00:01:12.708
<i>Shout out your feelings! (shout!)</i>

00:01:12.708 --> 00:01:13.458
<i>Isn't it fine</i>

00:01:13.458 --> 00:01:15.583
<i>if nothing is for sure?</i>

00:01:15.583 --> 00:01:16.625
<i>wow yeah!</i>

00:01:16.625 --> 00:01:17.125
<i>That's right</i>

00:01:17.125 --> 00:01:18.958
<i>Let's put away the lies</i>

00:01:18.958 --> 00:01:21.667
<i>Let lots of love reach you</i>

00:01:26.167 --> 00:01:28.583
<i>Let lots of love reach you</i>

00:01:37.667 --> 00:01:41.125
"Blue Flame"

00:01:41.125 --> 00:01:44.125
"Blue Flame"
"Start outside the Tsukino dorms.

00:01:44.125 --> 00:01:47.708
The two MCs say opening greetings and
talk about what they've been doing recently...

00:01:47.708 --> 00:01:49.750
Unscripted talk for a while."

00:01:56.417 --> 00:02:00.333
I've gotten used to
unscripted talking on the radio,

00:02:00.333 --> 00:02:04.417
but I don't have much experience
with this kind of variety show.

00:02:04.417 --> 00:02:10.458
After getting into show business, I've been
singing and doing a lot of different kinds of work.

00:02:14.458 --> 00:02:17.250
And one day, I'm sure...

00:02:21.917 --> 00:02:23.958
Good morning.

00:02:23.958 --> 00:02:25.958
Good morning!

00:02:25.958 --> 00:02:28.833
I'm Aoi Satsuki from Six Gravity.

00:02:28.833 --> 00:02:31.250
I'm Koi Kisaragi. Call me "Koi!"

00:02:31.250 --> 00:02:34.208
Ah, Koi. Shh!

00:02:34.208 --> 00:02:38.167
Oh, right. "Shh."

00:02:38.167 --> 00:02:40.375
You sure are energetic this morning, Koi.

00:02:40.375 --> 00:02:44.542
Yes, Aoi! I'm really excited about this program!

00:02:44.542 --> 00:02:47.917
Looks like you checked your
script carefully yesterday, huh?

00:02:47.917 --> 00:02:49.458
Are you ready?

00:02:49.458 --> 00:02:51.875
Yes, leave it to me!

00:02:51.875 --> 00:02:53.833
I love variety shows.

00:02:53.833 --> 00:02:56.542
I'm all fired up, too. I'll do my best!

00:02:56.542 --> 00:02:58.375
What about you, Aoi?

00:02:58.375 --> 00:03:02.833
I wonder if it's really okay
to do something like this...

00:03:02.833 --> 00:03:06.958
Now that we're here, we just need to do it, Aoi!

00:03:06.958 --> 00:03:11.333
So anyway, we're here at...

00:03:13.333 --> 00:03:18.167
...the Tsukino dorms,
where Gravi and Procella live!

00:03:18.167 --> 00:03:20.500
And the time right now is...

00:03:20.500 --> 00:03:22.417
6 a.m.!

00:03:23.833 --> 00:03:26.333
Koi, you're definitely not
usually awake at this time, huh?

00:03:26.333 --> 00:03:30.042
I can definitely vouch for that.

00:03:30.042 --> 00:03:31.750
You'd vouch for it, huh?

00:03:31.750 --> 00:03:33.292
Well...

00:03:34.333 --> 00:03:38.333
I could also be still awake after
swimming through the ocean of the internet.

00:03:38.333 --> 00:03:42.125
That's... staying up a little too late...

00:03:42.125 --> 00:03:44.208
Hajime would get mad at you.

00:03:44.208 --> 00:03:47.708
Well, let's say it's the true
pleasure of summer vacation...

00:03:47.708 --> 00:03:50.250
...when I don't have work the next day...

00:03:50.250 --> 00:03:52.583
Yes, let's do that.

00:03:52.583 --> 00:03:55.667
This is the first time a
camera's been inside here, huh?

00:03:55.667 --> 00:03:59.875
Yeah. But it's a place we're used to seeing.

00:03:59.875 --> 00:04:03.208
And, this is what we're doing here...

00:04:03.583 --> 00:04:05.583
"Showing publicly for the first time!
Gravi/Procella members as they wake up!!"

00:04:05.625 --> 00:04:08.458
I can't believe the agency said okay to this.

00:04:08.458 --> 00:04:13.542
That's, well, because there are so many fans
who want a look at our private lives.

00:04:13.542 --> 00:04:16.375
Isn't that what they were responding to?

00:04:16.375 --> 00:04:17.708
I wonder if it'll be okay...

00:04:17.708 --> 00:04:19.042
What?

00:04:19.042 --> 00:04:23.708
I was just wondering if it was okay
to show everyone when they're not "on."

00:04:23.708 --> 00:04:26.083
I guess that was my conscience talking.

00:04:26.083 --> 00:04:30.958
Aoi, as long as we're idols, we need
to respond to the fans' voices!

00:04:30.958 --> 00:04:33.250
Now, come on, let's go!

00:04:34.458 --> 00:04:36.125
I wonder if it'll be okay...

00:04:39.542 --> 00:04:41.000
Sorry to intrude!

00:04:41.000 --> 00:04:43.750
That's a weird greeting for this situation...

00:04:43.750 --> 00:04:46.375
Good morning.

00:04:46.375 --> 00:04:50.708
The man earlier was the doorkeeper
who protects this dorm.

00:04:50.708 --> 00:04:55.333
There is also a guard who patrols
during the day, so the security's perfect.

00:04:55.333 --> 00:04:58.125
This <i>is </i>a dorm for celebrities, after all.

00:04:58.125 --> 00:05:02.042
So it's hard to get inside, huh?

00:05:02.042 --> 00:05:05.417
It's a five-story building in
a certain place in the city.

00:05:05.417 --> 00:05:07.500
Our seniors in the same agency also live here.

00:05:07.500 --> 00:05:12.417
The second floor is the Gravi floor,
and the third floor is for Procella.

00:05:14.458 --> 00:05:17.625
Someone's coming down! Staff, hide...!

00:05:19.917 --> 00:05:22.792
Oh? What are you guys doing
so early in the morning?

00:05:22.792 --> 00:05:24.917
Oh, there's a camera, too.

00:05:24.917 --> 00:05:26.083
Shh!

00:05:26.083 --> 00:05:28.083
"Shh"?

00:05:28.083 --> 00:05:31.458
Oh, is this a candid wake-up call?

00:05:31.458 --> 00:05:32.750
Yeah.

00:05:32.750 --> 00:05:35.792
Oh, nice! That sounds interesting.

00:05:35.792 --> 00:05:38.917
Oh, I shouldn't get in the way
of your filming, huh?

00:05:38.917 --> 00:05:40.458
Well, good luck!

00:05:40.792 --> 00:05:46.042
Even for a healthy kid, he's up too early.

00:05:46.042 --> 00:05:47.417
I want to learn from him.

00:05:47.417 --> 00:05:48.667
You should.

00:05:48.667 --> 00:05:50.750
I will look into it proactively!

00:05:50.750 --> 00:05:52.167
Hey!

00:05:53.417 --> 00:05:55.250
What are you two doing?

00:05:55.250 --> 00:05:57.417
Oh, this is...

00:05:57.417 --> 00:05:58.458
...a candid wake-up call.

00:05:58.458 --> 00:05:59.833
Oh, is that right?

00:05:59.833 --> 00:06:03.750
Sorry. Should I go back to my
room and pretend to be asleep?

00:06:03.750 --> 00:06:06.208
Oh, no, we're not doing fake ones...

00:06:06.208 --> 00:06:10.417
It's fine, it just means we've
already failed with two...

00:06:10.417 --> 00:06:12.417
I see. Sorry 'bout that.

00:06:12.417 --> 00:06:13.583
See ya!

00:06:13.583 --> 00:06:16.375
The Procella team wakes up too early...

00:06:16.375 --> 00:06:18.625
Hmm... I really want to
proactively learn from them!

00:06:22.250 --> 00:06:24.375
Good morning.

00:06:24.375 --> 00:06:26.250
Maybe we shouldn't do this after all...

00:06:26.250 --> 00:06:28.625
Aoi, this is upstanding work, too.

00:06:28.625 --> 00:06:29.667
Let's do our best.

00:06:29.667 --> 00:06:33.083
You're right... It's work... work...

00:06:33.083 --> 00:06:36.625
Okay, then we'll start with You's room.

00:06:40.583 --> 00:06:42.000
This way, this way.

00:07:02.500 --> 00:07:04.375
Whoa, there are a lot of books about curry.

00:07:04.375 --> 00:07:08.583
I'd heard he did a lot of research,
but this is amazing.

00:07:08.583 --> 00:07:10.542
"Yakiniku sauce (medium hot), Chutney, Chocolate,
White chocolate, Ketchup, Yogurt, Garlic"

00:07:10.542 --> 00:07:12.833
Is this a curry recipe?

00:07:12.833 --> 00:07:16.167
You can really tell how much he likes curry, huh?

00:07:29.000 --> 00:07:30.333
He's still sleeping, huh?

00:07:30.333 --> 00:07:33.333
Well, I think You's a pretty deep sleeper.

00:07:33.333 --> 00:07:34.500
In that case...

00:07:34.500 --> 00:07:36.667
Wh-What are you doing?

00:07:36.667 --> 00:07:38.125
Excuse me...

00:07:38.125 --> 00:07:40.250
Don't do that! He'll wake up!

00:07:40.250 --> 00:07:43.083
Sorry, I suddenly got sleepy.

00:07:43.083 --> 00:07:44.708
I'll leave the rest to you, Aoi.

00:07:44.708 --> 00:07:45.750
Good nigh--

00:07:50.417 --> 00:07:51.458
Huh?

00:07:58.417 --> 00:08:01.750
W-W-Wait, you can't air this!

00:08:05.958 --> 00:08:08.208
Good morning.

00:08:08.208 --> 00:08:10.583
Oh, it's just you, Koi?

00:08:12.875 --> 00:08:15.083
What do you mean, "it's just you"?!

00:08:15.083 --> 00:08:17.208
Who did you want it to be, then?

00:08:17.208 --> 00:08:18.500
Jeez!

00:08:18.500 --> 00:08:20.458
S-Sorry about that.

00:08:20.458 --> 00:08:23.792
The agency definitely won't approve this scene...

00:08:25.583 --> 00:08:27.958
Now, our next target is--

00:08:27.958 --> 00:08:31.500
We spent too much time in You's room,
so we have to hurry a little.

00:08:31.500 --> 00:08:34.542
We can't do that.
The Kakerun fans won't accept it.

00:08:34.542 --> 00:08:36.542
We have to give it our all.

00:08:39.542 --> 00:08:42.292
We don't have to hold back since it's Kakeru.

00:08:42.292 --> 00:08:44.542
Is that really the issue here?

00:08:47.875 --> 00:08:49.583
Good morning!

00:08:49.583 --> 00:08:51.500
Good morning.

00:08:54.458 --> 00:08:56.167
Kakeru, morning!

00:08:57.333 --> 00:08:58.917
I'm sleepy...

00:08:58.917 --> 00:09:04.958
Kakeru, if you don't wake up soon,
your precious point cards might get taken away.

00:09:04.958 --> 00:09:06.958
Wait a minute!

00:09:08.958 --> 00:09:11.542
Huh? It's only 6 o'clock...

00:09:12.958 --> 00:09:15.583
Oh, there's a cameraman.

00:09:15.583 --> 00:09:19.167
Oh, and Koi and Aoi. What's the matter?

00:09:20.417 --> 00:09:22.792
M-Morning, Kakeru...

00:09:22.792 --> 00:09:25.542
Kakeru, you're too awake already.

00:09:25.542 --> 00:09:27.458
It's ruining this segment.

00:09:27.458 --> 00:09:29.208
Huh? "Segment"?

00:09:29.333 --> 00:09:31.250
"Candid Wake-Up Call
A huge success!"

00:09:32.750 --> 00:09:34.667
A huge success!

00:09:37.792 --> 00:09:40.542
Next is Rui's room.

00:09:44.583 --> 00:09:45.875
Poke, poke.

00:09:53.875 --> 00:09:55.375
Retreat!

00:10:01.917 --> 00:10:04.750
His bedhead is artistic as usual.

00:10:04.750 --> 00:10:07.500
We have to fix it for him later.

00:10:07.500 --> 00:10:09.292
Here we go!

00:10:12.292 --> 00:10:13.875
Ready, pose!

00:10:20.792 --> 00:10:23.958
We're finally at Shun's room.

00:10:23.958 --> 00:10:26.875
We're challenging this
unexplored land at last, huh?

00:10:26.875 --> 00:10:28.500
Well then, please do the honors.

00:10:28.500 --> 00:10:29.917
All right.

00:10:31.708 --> 00:10:33.667
Wh-Wh-Wh-What the heck?

00:10:33.667 --> 00:10:36.042
Is this a door to another dimension?
An anywhere door?

00:10:36.042 --> 00:10:38.917
I-It's just your imagination.
Look, this time--

00:10:45.375 --> 00:10:46.875
Retreat!

00:10:46.875 --> 00:10:48.083
Yes, sir!

00:10:48.083 --> 00:10:49.958
"After the commercial will be
a grand infiltration of Hajime's room!?"

00:10:55.875 --> 00:10:58.042
Now, next is...

00:10:58.042 --> 00:11:00.458
...our leader's room, right?

00:11:00.458 --> 00:11:04.833
Oh? What are you doing
so early in the morning?

00:11:04.833 --> 00:11:09.208
Aw... Haru, you found us. Good morning.

00:11:09.208 --> 00:11:11.042
Good morning.

00:11:11.042 --> 00:11:16.000
Don't tell me you two are planning on
doing a candid wake-up call on Hajime?

00:11:16.000 --> 00:11:17.375
Yes.

00:11:17.375 --> 00:11:19.667
For the Hajime Mutsuki fans!

00:11:22.042 --> 00:11:23.417
Trust me.

00:11:23.417 --> 00:11:25.042
You shouldn't do this.

00:11:25.042 --> 00:11:27.125
Why not?

00:11:27.125 --> 00:11:29.375
That's what I was thinking...

00:11:29.375 --> 00:11:30.125
What?

00:11:30.125 --> 00:11:33.250
But what about the show?

00:11:33.250 --> 00:11:35.875
Koi, you aren't scared of anything, are you?

00:11:35.875 --> 00:11:38.000
I'll pass on this one...

00:11:38.000 --> 00:11:40.250
What? Why?

00:11:40.250 --> 00:11:41.833
I mean...

00:11:41.833 --> 00:11:44.000
Right, Haru?

00:11:44.000 --> 00:11:45.417
Yes.

00:11:46.500 --> 00:11:49.458
Fine. I will go by myself.

00:11:49.458 --> 00:11:52.458
I will carry out the mission even if I am alone!

00:11:59.125 --> 00:12:00.417
It's about time, I think?

00:12:03.208 --> 00:12:05.250
That's why I told him...

00:12:05.250 --> 00:12:06.792
Yeah.

00:12:08.375 --> 00:12:12.417
This is the place that feeds us.

00:12:12.417 --> 00:12:15.250
Thank you for always providing delicious food!

00:12:15.250 --> 00:12:18.083
Usually, a chef prepares the food,

00:12:18.083 --> 00:12:21.250
but sometimes the group members
who like to cook also do so here.

00:12:22.250 --> 00:12:23.667
Morning, Yoru!

00:12:25.375 --> 00:12:27.292
Good morning, Yoru!

00:12:27.292 --> 00:12:29.583
Even though your name means
"night," you wake up early, huh?

00:12:29.583 --> 00:12:33.500
I've heard that over a thousand times already.

00:12:34.917 --> 00:12:37.083
Oh? What are you doing?

00:12:37.083 --> 00:12:39.250
I'm making miso soup.

00:12:39.250 --> 00:12:40.750
Miso soup...

00:12:42.583 --> 00:12:45.292
I'm still not used to the Kanto area's flavoring,

00:12:45.292 --> 00:12:48.917
so sometimes I have them
let me make the miso soup.

00:12:55.500 --> 00:12:59.125
You wake up early just to make miso soup?

00:12:59.125 --> 00:13:01.833
And from scratch, too.

00:13:01.833 --> 00:13:07.417
It's more flavorful when you make the soup stock
from bonito flakes and dried sardines.

00:13:07.417 --> 00:13:11.458
I'll be in the way if I don't finish
before the chef comes,

00:13:11.458 --> 00:13:13.000
so it's better if I make it early in the morning.

00:13:16.042 --> 00:13:18.292
It's delicious!

00:13:18.792 --> 00:13:20.875
Procella's mornings are early.

00:13:20.875 --> 00:13:23.000
Huh? What did you say?

00:13:23.000 --> 00:13:25.792
Procella's mornings are early.

00:13:27.208 --> 00:13:29.000
R-Right...

00:13:31.208 --> 00:13:34.083
Ta-da! This is...!

00:13:34.083 --> 00:13:36.042
Is the camera really going in?

00:13:36.042 --> 00:13:38.042
Of course it is!

00:13:38.792 --> 00:13:40.125
Door, open!

00:13:40.125 --> 00:13:42.708
This is Aoi's room!

00:13:44.083 --> 00:13:48.375
I expect no less! This room is so neat.

00:13:48.375 --> 00:13:51.833
I'd rather you didn't look so carefully...

00:13:51.833 --> 00:13:53.917
Oh, here's your bookshelf--

00:13:53.917 --> 00:13:55.708
Man, you barely have any manga!

00:13:55.708 --> 00:13:57.208
It's mostly novels...

00:13:57.208 --> 00:14:03.167
Other than that, there are cookbooks
and books dealing with animals and pets.

00:14:03.167 --> 00:14:05.500
Well, I like reading.

00:14:05.500 --> 00:14:09.917
When I wander into a bookstore,
I usually end up buying a few books.

00:14:09.917 --> 00:14:12.208
Recently, I've just been adding
to my to-read pile, though.

00:14:12.208 --> 00:14:14.958
There are a lot I haven't read yet.

00:14:14.958 --> 00:14:17.833
Oh, peace of mind from just buying, huh?

00:14:17.833 --> 00:14:19.083
I understand that feeling.

00:14:19.083 --> 00:14:22.000
You have a lot of different genres, though.

00:14:22.000 --> 00:14:24.792
How many cookbooks do you have?

00:14:24.792 --> 00:14:27.375
"Things to Learn When Cooking Japanese Food,"

00:14:27.375 --> 00:14:29.375
"Simple Tips for Cooking Chinese Food,"

00:14:29.375 --> 00:14:31.417
and "Easy Italian Cooking."

00:14:31.417 --> 00:14:33.792
Oh, this bread looks good!

00:14:33.792 --> 00:14:38.250
Oh, focaccia can be made in a pot,
so I'll make it for you sometime.

00:14:38.250 --> 00:14:41.167
It's delicious with a little olive oil.

00:14:41.167 --> 00:14:44.167
Huh? You can make bread in a pot?

00:14:44.167 --> 00:14:46.917
Yup, as long as you have some parchment paper.

00:14:46.917 --> 00:14:52.417
If we let the dough rest in the fridge,
it'll take some time to rise, but it's easy.

00:14:52.417 --> 00:14:54.750
Aoi, you're too conscientious.

00:14:54.750 --> 00:14:57.375
You're going to max out your homemaker skills.

00:14:58.167 --> 00:14:59.625
Next, this is--

00:14:59.625 --> 00:15:01.792
Aw, are you really going in?

00:15:01.792 --> 00:15:03.792
You don't seem unhappy about this at all.

00:15:03.792 --> 00:15:06.083
In fact, you look like there's
something you want to show off!

00:15:07.292 --> 00:15:08.833
Just a little something.

00:15:08.833 --> 00:15:11.125
So there <i>is </i>something? I knew it.

00:15:11.125 --> 00:15:12.417
I'm going in!

00:15:12.417 --> 00:15:13.792
Go ahead.

00:15:13.792 --> 00:15:15.667
You really are happy about this, huh?

00:15:16.667 --> 00:15:19.542
Wow, did you get more figures again?

00:15:19.542 --> 00:15:23.625
I think I have twice as many that
are still in their boxes in the back.

00:15:23.625 --> 00:15:25.958
You're buying too many.

00:15:25.958 --> 00:15:28.042
B-But if you miss your chance
to get limited editions,

00:15:28.042 --> 00:15:31.208
you might never be able to get them!

00:15:31.208 --> 00:15:33.208
I understand how you feel, though.

00:15:33.208 --> 00:15:36.167
Let's see... Which is your favorite?

00:15:36.167 --> 00:15:38.250
Right now, it's this one!

00:15:38.250 --> 00:15:40.042
The second season of the anime
that's airing soon--

00:15:40.042 --> 00:15:45.292
Super Dimension Mobile Robot:
Ultimate Black Wing's Hyper Model Custom X!

00:15:45.292 --> 00:15:49.542
I can't tell how much of that was the title
and how much was the name...

00:15:49.542 --> 00:15:53.750
This is the model that only came out at the end
of the last episode of the first season.

00:15:53.750 --> 00:15:56.625
And it's the Custom X type
with the reinforced weapons.

00:15:56.625 --> 00:15:59.875
Oh, rather than listen to me explain,
let's see the real thing!

00:15:59.875 --> 00:16:02.083
I have it all recorded!

00:16:02.083 --> 00:16:04.125
Yeah, okay.

00:16:08.542 --> 00:16:09.958
At this rate...

00:16:21.000 --> 00:16:22.333
Can you hear me?

00:16:26.250 --> 00:16:30.625
Now is the time to use those
reinforced parts that we developed in secret!

00:16:30.625 --> 00:16:32.417
Release Custom X!

00:16:39.917 --> 00:16:41.958
Look, this is it! This!

00:16:41.958 --> 00:16:44.333
Isn't this the best?!

00:16:44.333 --> 00:16:45.667
I guess...

00:16:52.167 --> 00:16:53.792
It's so cool!

00:16:54.500 --> 00:16:56.750
What is this blue flame?

00:16:59.167 --> 00:17:03.417
Did you see that?
The gallant figure of Hyper Model X?

00:17:05.167 --> 00:17:11.500
Oh no! I've never flown this
powered up model before...!

00:17:11.667 --> 00:17:13.750
"The End"

00:17:13.750 --> 00:17:14.708
"The End"
It ends here?

00:17:14.708 --> 00:17:16.125
"The End"
Keep watching!

00:17:16.125 --> 00:17:18.000
"The End"
"Second season coming!"

00:17:18.333 --> 00:17:22.250
It's so sneaky! To make it so exciting
and then end it like this!

00:17:22.250 --> 00:17:25.500
I <i>have </i>to know what happens next!

00:17:25.500 --> 00:17:30.083
Even so, we can't assume that there was
always going to be a second season, right?

00:17:30.083 --> 00:17:34.458
They green-lit a second season because of
the heartfelt support of us fans!

00:17:34.458 --> 00:17:37.250
I'm getting all fired up!

00:17:37.250 --> 00:17:39.083
He's so lucky, riding a Black Wing.

00:17:39.083 --> 00:17:41.917
I wish I could ride one just once.

00:17:43.375 --> 00:17:48.292
Voice actors consider playing a
Black Wing pilot to be a kind of status symbol,

00:17:48.292 --> 00:17:52.250
and I heard all the past voice actors
for Black Wing pilots have said,

00:17:52.250 --> 00:17:56.458
"This is my Black Wing" in front of the figures.

00:17:56.458 --> 00:17:58.500
They're so lucky! I'm jealous!

00:17:58.500 --> 00:17:59.667
I see.

00:17:59.667 --> 00:18:01.917
Right? Isn't it amazing?

00:18:01.917 --> 00:18:05.000
But can this even be aired on TV?

00:18:05.000 --> 00:18:07.708
They might be on different
stations or something...

00:18:07.708 --> 00:18:08.708
Oh.

00:18:11.250 --> 00:18:14.042
And here we are having our morning meetings.

00:18:14.042 --> 00:18:19.458
We confirm the jobs for the day
as we eat together.

00:18:20.833 --> 00:18:24.375
But man, the two groups are so different.

00:18:24.375 --> 00:18:27.125
Procella's really free...

00:18:28.042 --> 00:18:31.792
"Lettuce"

00:18:32.708 --> 00:18:33.958
"Candid Wake-Up Call
A huge success!"

00:18:33.958 --> 00:18:36.792
That's it for our report from the Tsukino dorms!

00:18:36.792 --> 00:18:40.292
Thank you for watching!

00:18:40.292 --> 00:18:42.417
Okay, good work!

00:18:42.417 --> 00:18:44.250
Good work.

00:18:45.292 --> 00:18:47.792
You're not airing <i>that</i>, right?

00:18:53.792 --> 00:18:55.875
What?! Really?

00:18:55.875 --> 00:18:56.875
Yes.

00:18:56.875 --> 00:19:00.458
Apparently, the director liked that program
introducing the Tsukino dorms,

00:19:00.458 --> 00:19:03.625
so he made the offer himself.

00:19:03.625 --> 00:19:07.167
We can fit it into your schedule.
What do you want to do?

00:19:07.167 --> 00:19:08.917
I'll do it! I can do it!

00:19:08.917 --> 00:19:11.042
I mean, please let me do it!

00:19:11.042 --> 00:19:15.125
Please let me record for Super Dimension
Mobile Robot: Ultimate Black Wing!

00:19:48.292 --> 00:19:50.833
He's studying his script so diligently!

00:19:50.833 --> 00:19:53.833
I've never seen him this focused before.

00:19:53.833 --> 00:19:55.792
He must be really fired up about this.

00:20:00.417 --> 00:20:02.542
With this line, how will I...

00:20:02.542 --> 00:20:04.667
If you decide too much about
a character beforehand,

00:20:04.667 --> 00:20:06.833
you might have problems when recording,

00:20:06.833 --> 00:20:10.000
so it might be better if you
only decided up to a certain extent.

00:20:10.000 --> 00:20:11.083
It's okay!

00:20:11.083 --> 00:20:13.833
I've planned more than ten ways to act this out!

00:20:13.833 --> 00:20:16.250
O-Oh, really...?

00:20:16.250 --> 00:20:17.792
Do your best.

00:20:17.792 --> 00:20:18.917
I will!

00:20:26.125 --> 00:20:26.500
"Super Dimension Mobile Robot:
Ultimate Black Wing"

00:20:26.500 --> 00:20:29.083
Koi Kisaragi is coming in!

00:20:29.083 --> 00:20:30.417
Good morning!

00:20:30.417 --> 00:20:34.958
I will do my best today with
all my heart and everything I have!

00:20:34.958 --> 00:20:36.833
I look forward to working with you!

00:20:36.833 --> 00:20:38.167
Looking forward to it.

00:20:40.958 --> 00:20:42.792
Are the headphones okay?

00:20:42.792 --> 00:20:44.875
Yes, they're fine!

00:20:44.875 --> 00:20:46.917
Okay, then I'll play it once.

00:20:46.917 --> 00:20:48.125
Please do!

00:20:57.583 --> 00:21:00.125
Then let's do a dry run.

00:21:02.042 --> 00:21:04.625
Okay, let's record.

00:21:04.625 --> 00:21:05.625
Yes, sir!

00:21:05.625 --> 00:21:07.042
Here we go.

00:21:08.417 --> 00:21:09.917
"Line"

00:21:10.167 --> 00:21:10.667
"Line"

00:21:10.917 --> 00:21:11.667
"Line"

00:21:26.583 --> 00:21:28.000
What?

00:21:28.000 --> 00:21:30.000
That's all?

00:21:32.667 --> 00:21:35.208
What'd you think? Perfect, right?

00:21:39.500 --> 00:21:41.875
Y-Yeah...

00:21:42.458 --> 00:21:44.958
<i>The record we etched together</i>

00:21:44.958 --> 00:21:47.708
<i>Put away on a secret rack</i>

00:21:47.708 --> 00:21:50.417
<i>Lingering in the vision of dawn</i>

00:21:50.417 --> 00:21:55.875
<i>As I sleep lightly</i>

00:21:58.875 --> 00:22:04.083
<i>This must be the world I dreamed up</i>

00:22:04.083 --> 00:22:09.542
<i>This miniature garden of time</i>

00:22:09.542 --> 00:22:15.000
<i>The people passing by all look familiar</i>

00:22:15.000 --> 00:22:20.250
<i>Looking like the last time I saw them</i>

00:22:20.250 --> 00:22:25.750
<i>Taking a walk in the park</i>
<i>that used to be in front of the station</i>

00:22:25.750 --> 00:22:31.167
<i>I tried to look for you hanging decorations</i>

00:22:31.167 --> 00:22:33.833
<i>That clear voice</i>

00:22:33.833 --> 00:22:36.583
<i>My hand was always drawn to</i>

00:22:36.583 --> 00:22:43.125
<i>On a journey through my memories</i>

00:22:43.125 --> 00:22:45.667
<i>The record we etched together</i>

00:22:45.667 --> 00:22:48.417
<i>Listened to on repeat so much it's worn out</i>

00:22:48.417 --> 00:22:51.167
<i>It became unplayable some time ago</i>

00:22:51.167 --> 00:22:53.875
<i>And now it's just an object</i>

00:22:53.875 --> 00:22:56.542
<i>I can still see it on the back of my eyelids</i>

00:22:56.542 --> 00:22:59.292
<i>If I listen carefully, I can hear it</i>

00:22:59.292 --> 00:23:02.042
<i>As the seasons pass, and I grow older</i>

00:23:02.042 --> 00:23:08.250
<i>It grows dimmer, though</i>

00:23:11.917 --> 00:23:12.917
"Episode 11: Moment of Indecision"

00:23:12.917 --> 00:23:15.708
"Episode 11: Moment of Indecision"
I'm the Gravi leader, Hajime Mutsuki.

00:23:15.708 --> 00:23:19.083
"Episode 11: Moment of Indecision"
And I'm the Procella leader, Shun Shimotsuki.

00:23:19.083 --> 00:23:20.250
"Episode 11: Moment of Indecision"
Oh my, Hajime, are you

00:23:20.250 --> 00:23:22.042
"Episode 11: Moment of Indecision"
worried about something?

00:23:22.042 --> 00:23:25.375
"Episode 11: Moment of Indecision"
It's unusual to see the black king at a loss.

00:23:25.375 --> 00:23:29.167
But melancholy Hajime is charming, too.

00:23:29.167 --> 00:23:33.500
Now, why don't you pour your heart out to me?

00:23:33.500 --> 00:23:35.625
Be quiet.

00:23:35.625 --> 00:23:38.500
Next time, "Moment of Indecision."

00:23:38.500 --> 00:23:42.059
Hajime, go out on a date with me tonight.
